@startuml sequence-release
' Hand-maintained. Source of truth = .github/workflows/java-docker.yml + deploy-gitops.yml
' python-docker.yml runs the identical sequence — only the build step differs (pack build).
title Push to main — build, pin to digest, sign, verify, promote

autonumber
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true

participant "java-docker.yml\nbuild-and-push" as D <<release>>
participant "Maven + Paketo\nspring-boot:build-image" as MVN
database "GHCR" as GHCR
participant "Trivy" as TRIVY
participant "Syft" as SYFT
participant "Cosign" as COSIGN
participant "Sigstore\nfulcio · rekor · tuf" as SIGSTORE <<external>>
participant "deploy-gitops.yml\nupdate-manifest" as G <<release>>
participant "k8s manifest" as MANIFEST
participant "Argo CD" as ARGO <<consumer side>>

D -> MVN : package spring-boot:build-image\n-Dspring-boot.build-image.publish=true
note right of MVN
  Quality plugins skipped — dedicated jobs
  already cover them: maven.test.skip,
  enforcer, spotless, jacoco, checkstyle.
end note
MVN -> GHCR : push ghcr.io/<owner>/<repo>:main-<sha7>

D -> D : Resolve image reference\ndocker inspect → RepoDigests[0]
alt digest is empty
  D -->> D : ::error:: + exit 1
  note right of D : Never promote what cannot be pinned.
end
note right of D
  From here on **every** step uses
  name@sha256:… — never the mutable tag.
  A tag repointed between build and deploy
  cannot slip through.
end note

D -> TRIVY : scan image @digest\nCRITICAL,HIGH · ignore-unfixed · exit-code 1
note right of TRIVY
  DB restored from a per-UTC-date cache;
  saved only on main. Honors the consumer's
  root .trivyignore.
end note

D -> SYFT : SBOM @digest (cyclonedx-json)
SYFT --> D : sbom.cyclonedx.json
D -> D : upload artifact (30 days)

D -> COSIGN : cosign sign --yes @digest
COSIGN -> SIGSTORE : OIDC (id-token: write) → cert + rekor entry
note right of COSIGN
  Keyless: no long-lived keys. The SAN is
  always .../Bigorno12/ci-cd-templates/…
  because signing runs INSIDE the template
  repo, whoever called it.
end note
D -> COSIGN : cosign attest --type cyclonedx --predicate sbom @digest
COSIGN -> SIGSTORE : in-toto attestation
D -> GHCR : ghcr-cleanup — keep 3 most recent (retry once after 60s)

D --> G : output image-digest

group Verification gate — runs BEFORE any checkout or commit
  G -> GHCR : docker login (CR_PAT || github.token)
  G -> COSIGN : cosign verify @digest\n--certificate-identity-regexp $IDENTITY\n--certificate-oidc-issuer token.actions.githubusercontent.com
  COSIGN -> SIGSTORE : fetch cert + verify inclusion
  alt digest empty OR signature/identity mismatch
    G -->> G : exit 1 — manifest untouched
  end
end
note right of G
  IDENTITY defaults to
  ^https://github\.com/<owner>/[^/]+/\.github/workflows/
  which only matches inside the Bigorno12 org.
  Cross-org consumers MUST pin
  signer-identity-regexp or the gate fails closed.
end note

G -> G : checkout (persist-credentials: true,\nGITOPS_PAT || github.token)
G -> MANIFEST : sed image: ghcr.io/<repo>:… → :main-<sha7>
alt manifest changed
  G -> MANIFEST : commit "chore(gitops): update image tag … [skip ci]" + push
else no diff
  G -> G : "No manifest changes detected."
end
MANIFEST --> ARGO : auto-sync (prune + self-heal)

note over D, MANIFEST
  **python-docker.yml is the same sequence.** Only step 1
  differs: `pack build --publish` replaces Maven + Paketo,
  and the digest is read back with `docker buildx imagetools
  inspect` because pack --publish leaves nothing in the local
  daemon. Trivy → Syft → cosign sign → attest → deploy-gitops
  are byte-identical, and deploy-gitops.yml is the same file.
end note

footer docs/sequence-release.puml — Bigorno12/ci-cd-templates
@enduml
